# 4-bit MLX weights. The everyday model; Shift+Tab adds thinking, and pi
# sends sampling to match the level, so this file's values are the fallback
# for `ollama run` outside pi.
# Sampling values are Qwen's published instruct-mode settings — wrong sampling
# hurts these models more than quantisation does.
FROM qwen3.8:27b-mlx
# 40960, not 65536. Ollama's own vram-based recommendation at a 40 GiB wired
# limit is 32768, and running at double that left roughly 14 GB for prefix-cache
# snapshots. Each snapshot at 30K depth is about 3.3 GB, so a handful filled it
# and Ollama freed the whole cache: measured 14 times in one afternoon, each
# costing a full re-prefill of 27-31K tokens, 190 to 220 seconds before the
# first output token. A session spent 34 minutes on 98 seconds of generation.
#
# At 40960 the model needs about 23 GB, leaving 17 GB for snapshots that are
# 60% the size, so roughly three times as many fit. phi's compaction trigger
# follows the window automatically and lands at 28,672.
PARAMETER num_ctx 40960
PARAMETER temperature 0.7
PARAMETER top_p 0.8
PARAMETER top_k 20
PARAMETER presence_penalty 1.5
